  "id": "COMPOUND:18839 - PROTEIN:4928",
  "verbalization": "Plakortide N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Plakortide N acts as a target for several compounds, which in turn target CD3 via different molecular pathways. Specifically, Plakortide N is linked to Malme-3M, a molecule that is a target of Opposit-4(15)-Ene-1Beta,11-Diol and 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid, both of which ultimately target CD3. This indicates that Plakortide N may influence CD3 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving receptor engagement or signaling pathways. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, relationship, highlighting the role of these compounds in modulating CD3 function. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the biological network and the potential for Plakortide N to be a key player in CD3-mediated cellular responses.",
